body:
### Description

When using a model like o3 with the webSearchPreview tool and the reasoning summary is enabled, you can see the actual search query o3 writes.
It would be very helpful to get this info to the frontend so that it can be displayed to the user.

```typescript
import OpenAI from "openai";

const openai = new OpenAI();

const response = await openai.responses.create({
  model: "o3-2025-04-16",
  input: [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "input_text",
          "text": "What will be added in the next version of the Vercel AI SDK",
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
  text: {
    "format": {
      "type": "text",
    },
  },
  reasoning: {
    "effort": "medium",
    "summary": "auto",
  },
  tools: [
    {
      "type": "web_search_preview",
      "user_location": {
        "type": "approximate",
      },
      "search_context_size": "medium",
    },
  ],
  streaming: true,
  store: true,
});

for await (const chunk of response) {
  console.log(JSON.stringify(chunk, null, 2));
}
```

Will print steps like this:
```json
{
  "type": "response.output_item.added",
  "sequence_number": 112,
  "output_index": 3,
  "item": {
    "id": "ws_68755c8903d8819c80181f01d8e7803f035a165df43f3ddd",
    "type": "web_search_call",
    "status": "in_progress"
  }
}
{
  "type": "response.web_search_call.in_progress",
  "sequence_number": 113,
  "output_index": 3,
  "item_id": "ws_68755c8903d8819c80181f01d8e7803f035a165df43f3ddd"
}
{
  "type": "response.web_search_call.searching",
  "sequence_number": 114,
  "output_index": 3,
  "item_id": "ws_68755c8903d8819c80181f01d8e7803f035a165df43f3ddd"
}
{
  "type": "response.web_search_call.completed",
  "sequence_number": 115,
  "output_index": 3,
  "item_id": "ws_68755c8903d8819c80181f01d8e7803f035a165df43f3ddd"
}
{
  "type": "response.output_item.done",
  "sequence_number": 116,
  "output_index": 3,
  "item": {
    "id": "ws_68755c8903d8819c80181f01d8e7803f035a165df43f3ddd",
    "type": "web_search_call",
    "status": "completed",
    "action": {
      "type": "search"
    }
  }
}
```

meaning the data is there, but when i replicate the same thing with the ai-sdk the `action` field gets lost.

I want to add that i call OpenAI through the ai-sdk like this:
```typescript

 const tools = {
  web_search_preview: openai.tools.webSearchPreview({
    searchContextSize: "medium",
  }),
};
  const result = streamText({
    model: openai.responses("o4-mini-2025-04-16"),
    providerOptions: {
      openai: {
        store: true,
        reasoningSummary: "detailed",
      },
    },
    tools,
    messages: convertToModelMessages(messages),
  });
```

### AI SDK Version

- ai: 5.0.0-beta.18
- @ai-sdk/openai 2.0.0-beta.7
